        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a976a3bf-1722-50f8-9653-5aeaeddda502",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Midnight Oil, Switchfoot\n- People: Peter Garrett, Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, Drew Shirley\n- Songs: \"Beds Are Burning\"\n- Albums: \"Diesel and Dust\"\n- Places: Sydney, San Diego, California\n- Topics: band formation, band membership\n\nFacts:\n- By late 1976, Peter Garrett moved to Sydney to complete his law degree, and Farm renamed itself Midnight Oil by drawing the new name from a hat.\n- Switchfoot is an American alternative rock band from San Diego, California.\n- Switchfoot's members are Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, and Drew Shirley.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" is a 1987 song by Midnight Oil and the first track on the album \"Diesel and Dust\".",
